Subject: [PATCH] council section: make the repository honest about its own
 defects at the top, not at item 31a

A reviewer landing cold read a confident Status block, worked down the page,
and only at contents item 31a discovered that the project believes its own
core offence cannot be pleaded. That ordering is an honesty defect of exactly
the kind this project does not tolerate elsewhere. Four fixes.

1. STATUS gains a 'Known defects' line, above 'Review': seven findings graded
   fatal, four in the tagged text, SEC. 6(a) named specifically, drafted
   responses located, and the conclusion stated -- v3.5 is a rebuild rather
   than a splice. A reader now meets the worst news in the first screen.

2. THE CORE READING SET puts the lane sweep SECOND, immediately after the
   statute, because reading the Act cold and discovering the sweep later is
   the wrong order for someone with fifteen hours. Errata, cure queue,
   companion and hostile brief renumber to third through sixth.

3. THE LANE BRIEFS are rewritten around what the seat is now for. They no
   longer ask 'do the elements hold' -- the sweep answered that. Each lane
   now states what the sweep found in that area, what has been drafted in
   response, and what the reviewer's questions actually are. Two lanes say
   plainly that their fixes are NOT drafted (security, fiscal) and one says
   only one of five is (open source), because a reviewer should know which
   findings are still open wounds.

4. THE TIME BUDGET is restated honestly. Ten to twenty hours was the figure
   for finding defects; verifying a sweep is different and can be bounded --
   the statute, your lane's section, then three findings verified or refuted
   with reasons. Six to eight hours for a complete, publishable disposition.

And the ask is stated where it belongs: a finding that the sweep is WRONG is
the most valuable disposition this project can receive, because we have acted
on it. A disposition refuting one finding is worth more than a full pass that
agrees with everything.

Tagged v3.4 text unchanged (E10).
